  <section class="rich-lesson-section" data-g7-u07-l02 aria-label="Grade 7 Adjacent Angles">
    <h3>Adjacent Angles — Edulytiks</h3>
    <h4>Source-aligned focus</h4><p>Use complementary and supplementary relationships to find unknown adjacent angles. Preserve the existing correct lesson body and use first-party diagrams or physical construction where appropriate.</p>
    <h4>Activity connection</h4><p>Cut rectangles, identify adjacent angle pairs, and distinguish sums of 90 and 180 degrees. Machine Practice checks only closed numerical or categorical subresults; drawing and geometric justification remain teacher reviewed.</p>
    <h4>Cool-down — first-party Edulytiks assessment</h4><p>One angle is 37 degrees. Find its complement and supplement. Draw or describe one adjacent construction for each and explain why the target sums differ.</p>
    <p><strong>Teacher review:</strong> Check construction accuracy, diagram labels, units, geometric justification, and written reasoning. This Cool-down is independently authored.</p>
  </section>
}

